      "text": "To find the value of the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\), we first identify the first term and the common difference of the sequence.\n\nThe first term \\(a_1\\) of the sequence is 2.\nThe common difference \\(d\\) is the difference between any two consecutive terms. For example, \\(5 - 2 = 3\\) and \\(8 - 5 = 3\\). Therefore, the common difference \\(d\\) is 3.\n\nThe general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\\]\n\nWe need to find the 25th term, so we substitute \\(n = 25\\), \\(a_1 = 2\\), and \\(d = 3\\) into the formula:\n\\[a_{25} = 2 + (25-1) \\cdot 3\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(25 - 1\\):\n\\[25 - 1 = 24\\]\n\nNext, multiply 24 by 3:\n\\[24 \\cdot 3 = 72\\]\n\nFinally, add 2 to 72:\n\\[2 + 72 = 74\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the 25th term is \\(\\boxed{74}\\).",
