      "text": "To find the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\), we first identify the first term (\\(a\\)) and the common difference (\\(d\\)) of the sequence.\n\n1. **Identify the first term (\\(a\\))**:\n   The first term of the sequence is \\(2\\).\n\n2. **Determine the common difference (\\(d\\))**:\n   The common difference is the difference between consecutive terms. We can calculate it as follows:\n   \\[\n   d = 5 - 2 = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence**:\n   The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   Here, \\(a_n\\) represents the \\(n\\)-th term, \\(a\\) is the first term, \\(d\\) is the common difference, and \\(n\\) is the term number.\n\n4. **Substitute the known values into the formula**:\n   We need to find the 25th term (\\(a_{25}\\)). Substituting \\(n = 25\\), \\(a = 2\\), and \\(d = 3\\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   a_{25} = 2 + (25-1) \\cdot 3\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the expression**:\n   \\[\n   a_{25} = 2 + 24 \\cdot 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a_{25} = 2 + 72\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a_{25} = 74\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence is \\(\\boxed{74}\\).",
